{"abstract":"Objective: To create a scalable and feasible retrospective consecutive knee osteoarthritis (OA) radiographic database with limited human labor using commercial and custom-built artificial intelligence (AI) tools. Methods: We applied four AI tools, two commercially available and two custom-built tools, to analyze 6 years of clinical consecutive knee radiographs from patients aged 35–79 at the University of Copenhagen Hospital, Bispebjerg-Frederiksberg Hospital, Denmark. The tools provided Kellgren-Lawrence (KL) grades, joint space widths, patella osteophyte detection, radiographic view detection, knee joint implant detection, and radiographic marker detection. Results: In total, 25,778 knee radiographs from 8575 patients were included in the database after excluding inapplicable radiographs, and 92.5% of the knees had a complete OA dataset. Using the four AI tools, we saved about 800 hours of radiologist reading time and only manually reviewed 16.0% of the images in the database. Conclusions: This study shows that clinical knee OA databases can be built using AI with limited human reading time for uniform grading and measurements. The concept is scalable temporally and across geographic regions and could help diversify further OA research by efficiently including radiographic knee OA data from different populations globally. We can prevent data dredging and overfitting OA theories on existing trite cohorts by including various gene pools and continuous expansion of new clinical cohorts. Furthermore, the suggested tools and applied approaches provide an ability to retest previous hypotheses and test new hypotheses on real-life clinical data with current disease prevalence and trends.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lenskjold, Anders","Brejnebøl, Mathias W.","Nybing, Janus U.","Rose, Martin H.","Gudbergsen, Henrik","Troelsen, Anders","Møller, Anne","Raaschou, Henriette","Boesen, Mikael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732350"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Feasibility study","Knee OA","Proof of concept"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Radiological Artificial Intelligence Testcenter, Copenhagen"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"constructing a clinical radiographic knee osteoarthritis database using artificial intelligence tools with limited human labor a proof of principle","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.joca.2023.11.014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-732350","identifier":[{"id":"38043857","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85179821464","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c59c2f0b-5da3-468e-a62b-ee7c2a792a9e"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Data diversity","Database creation","Feasibility study","Knee OA","Proof of concept"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9ED023C088947DE6C8A8189C0FACC018"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/383704025/1_s2.0_S1063458423009925_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.joca.2023.11.014","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Radiological Artificial Intelligence Testcenter, Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anders","key":"lenskjoldpau","last":"Lenskjold","name":"Lenskjold, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Mathias W.","key":"brejnebølpau","last":"Brejnebøl","locid":"3c4c8a53-926e-45fb-a7b4-990fc5eafed4","name":"Brejnebøl, Mathias W.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Janus U.","key":"nybingpau","last":"Nybing","name":"Nybing, Janus U.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Martin H.","key":"rosepau","last":"Rose","name":"Rose, Martin H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Henrik","key":"gudbergsenpau","last":"Gudbergsen","locid":"5cf9ab2f-2050-47b3-8651-0a5fd54dac76","name":"Gudbergsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2273-5337","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Anders","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"49cb6bcf-2ff6-41af-a356-a2a09c2ce7ba","name":"Troelsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0132-8182","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anne","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","locid":"d4ac7208-b372-4a21-9123-157b4bf3b02c","name":"Møller, Anne","name_org":"Moller, Anne","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-4108","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Henriette","key":"raaschoupau","last":"Raaschou","name":"Raaschou, Henriette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","first":"Mikael","key":"boesenpau","last":"Boesen","locid":"b449f652-d441-4b23-836f-2d5111ef64dd","name":"Boesen, Mikael","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38043857"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.joca.2023.11.014","issn":["10634584","15229653"],"issn_org":["10634584"],"issue":"3","journal":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage","pages":"310-318","status":"p","title":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179821464"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c59c2f0b-5da3-468e-a62b-ee7c2a792a9e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Constructing a clinical radiographic knee osteoarthritis database using artificial intelligence tools with limited human labor : A proof of principle","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732350","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Good outcomes in stroke care require swift diagnostics, for which magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) as first-line brain imaging is superior to computed tomography scans. Reduced length of stay (LOS) in hospital and emergency departments (ED) may optimize resource use. Fast-track stroke MRI was implemented as the primary imaging technique for suspected stroke, in the ED at Copenhagen University Hospital—Herlev and Gentofte in 2020. Objectives: We aimed to describe and compare LOS, MRI utilization, and the rate of strokes versus stroke-mimicking conditions on the stroke ward, before and after the implementation of fast-track MRI. Design and method: In this cross-sectional study, we used data from admissions to the neurologic ED and associated non-comprehensive stroke unit. We compared two time periods, that is, January 1–December 31, 2019, and January 1–December 31, 2020, before and after the implementation of fast-track stroke MRI. Results: There were 6650 admissions before and 7201 after implementation of fast-track stroke MRI. After implementation, we observed reductions in average LOS in hospitals from 56.0 to 38.6 h (p < 0.001), and LOS in ED from 9.17 to 8.63 h (p < 0.001). The use of inpatient MRI increased significantly, and the rate of acute ischemic stroke patients on the ward increased yet the rate of non-strokes remained unchanged. The association between shorter admissions and access to MRI remained (odds ratio 1.81, p < 0.001), after adjusting for sex, age, weekend admissions, and lockdown periods. Conclusion: Fast-track stroke MRI in ED associated with reduced LOS in hospital.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sagar, Malini Vendela","Gandrup, Karen Lind","Jensen, Diane","Krag, Christian Hedeager","Boesen, Mikael","Raaschou, Henriette","Christensen, Helle Collatz","Kruuse, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-790723"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Emergency department","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Stroke","Triage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient flow analysis with fast track mri for suspected stroke in the emergency department and associated non comprehensive stroke center","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/17562864241303251","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-790723","identifier":[{"id":"39668853","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11635884","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85212073153","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9d2e0aa8-1952-460f-8bd7-f4cbb0cae1f4"],"keyword":["admission length","emergency department","magnetic resonance imaging","stroke","stroke diagnostics","triage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C58CDE92517C831B224B994B464C2D12"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/416336716/sagar_et_al_2024_patient_flow_analysis_with_fast_track_mri_for_suspected_stroke_in_the_emergency_department_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/17562864241303251","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Malini Vendela","key":"sagarpau","last":"Sagar","name":"Sagar, Malini Vendela","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Karen Lind","key":"gandruppau","last":"Gandrup","name":"Gandrup, Karen Lind","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Diane","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Diane","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christian Hedeager","key":"kragpau","last":"Krag","name":"Krag, Christian Hedeager","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Mikael Ploug","key":"boesenpau","last":"Boesen","locid":"b449f652-d441-4b23-836f-2d5111ef64dd","name":"Boesen, Mikael","name_org":"Boesen, Mikael Ploug","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henriette","key":"raaschoupau","last":"Raaschou","name":"Raaschou, Henriette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Helle Collatz","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b05bae82-5e32-4f10-980c-147b4af03d6a","name":"Christensen, Helle Collatz","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christina","key":"kruusepau","last":"Kruuse","locid":"ddff4060-2809-4589-8d23-0eddfb7c5d6e","name":"Kruuse, Christina","orcid":"0000-0002-4210-0523","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39668853"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/17562864241303251","issn":["17562856","17562864"],"issn_org":["17562856"],"journal":"Therapeutic Advances in Neurological Disorders","status":"p","title":"Therapeutic Advances in Neurological Disorders","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212073153"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9d2e0aa8-1952-460f-8bd7-f4cbb0cae1f4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patient flow analysis with fast-track MRI for suspected stroke in the emergency department and associated non-comprehensive stroke center","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-790723","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To estimate the ability of a commercially available artificial intelligence (AI) tool to detect acute brain ischemia on Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), compared to an experienced neuroradiologist. Methods: We retrospectively included 1030 patients with brain MRI, suspected of stroke from January 6th, 2020 to 1st of April 2022, based on these criteria: Age ≥ 18 years, symptoms within four weeks before the scan. The neuroradiologist reinterpreted the MRI scans and subclassified ischemic lesions for reference. We excluded scans with interpretation difficulties due to artifacts or missing sequences. Four MRI scanner models from the same vendor were used. The first 800 patients were included consecutively, remaining enriched for less frequent lesions. The index test was a CE-approved AI tool (Apollo version 2.1.1 by Cerebriu). Results: The final analysis cohort comprised 995 patients (mean age 69 years, 53 % female). A case-based analysis for detecting acute ischemic lesions showed a sensitivity of 89 % (95 % CI: 85 %–91 %) and specificity of 90 % (95 % CI: 87 %–92 %). We found no significant difference in sensitivity or specificity based on sex, age, or comorbidities. Specificity was reduced in cases with DWI artifacts. Multivariate analysis showed that increasing ischemic lesion size and fragmented lesions were independently associated with higher sensitivity, while non-acute lesion ages lowered sensitivity. Conclusions: The AI tool exhibits high sensitivity and specificity in detecting acute ischemic lesions on MRI compared to an experienced neuroradiologist. While sensitivity depends on the ischemic lesions' characteristics, specificity depends on the image quality.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Krag, Christian H.","Müller, Felix C.","Gandrup, Karen L.","Raaschou, Henriette","Andersen, Michael Brun","Brejnebøl, Mathias W.","Sagar, Malini V.","Bojsen, Jonas A.","Rasmussen, Benjamin S.","Graumann, Ole","Nielsen, Mads","Kruuse, Christina","Boesen, Mikael"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-704573"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Krag, Christian H"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Diagnostic accuracy","Diffusion weighted imaging","Ischemic stroke","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Neuroradiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic test accuracy study of a commercially available deep learning algorithm for ischemic lesion detection on brain mris in suspected stroke patients from a non comprehensive stroke center","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/409206524/complete_article_clean_25_09_23.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-704573","identifier":[{"id":"37804650","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85173215282","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7339df10-44ad-419a-9159-977741c917d4","sdu-12a51d09-4995-4b88-9509-f8df2b160d61"],"keyword":["Artificial Intelligence","Diagnostic Accuracy","Diffusion Weighted Imaging","Ischemic Stroke","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Neuroradiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9743019BF0D09891B7FA56ADF259330D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/409206524/complete_article_clean_25_09_23.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Radiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christian H.","key":"kragpau","last":"Krag","name":"Krag, Christian H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Felix C.","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Felix C.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen L.","key":"gandruppau","last":"Gandrup","name":"Gandrup, Karen L.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henriette","key":"raaschoupau","last":"Raaschou","name":"Raaschou, Henriette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Michael B.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"2011438d-efaa-4cd0-a092-8e9970e0b885","name":"Andersen, Michael Brun","name_org":"Andersen, Michael B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias W.","key":"brejnebølpau","last":"Brejnebøl","name":"Brejnebøl, Mathias W.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malini V.","key":"sagarpau","last":"Sagar","name":"Sagar, Malini V.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas A","key":"bojsenpau","last":"Bojsen","locid":"81c40786-f06b-4b25-be8a-ee8e613fa0c7","name":"Bojsen, Jonas Asgaard","name_org":"Bojsen, Jonas A","orcid":"0000-0003-1603-462X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Benjamin S","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"1184a25b-a669-4b81-a271-62ac25d4255c","name":"Rasmussen, Benjamin Schnack","name_org":"Rasmussen, Benjamin S","orcid":"0000-0002-7357-0755","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"graumannpau","last":"Graumann","locid":"a700da97-54e6-4604-8507-6b507bd434fd","name":"Graumann, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-9663-8361","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mads","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52f8d6fb-fd83-4d11-ad65-3e183ca401f2","name":"Nielsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-1535-068X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christina","key":"kruusepau","last":"Kruuse","locid":"ddff4060-2809-4589-8d23-0eddfb7c5d6e","name":"Kruuse, Christina","orcid":"0000-0002-4210-0523","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Mikael","key":"boesenpau","last":"Boesen","locid":"b449f652-d441-4b23-836f-2d5111ef64dd","name":"Boesen, Mikael","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37804650"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejrad.2023.111126","issn":["0720048X","18727727"],"issn_org":["0720048X"],"journal":"European Journal of Radiology","paperid":"111126","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Radiology","volume":"168"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173215282"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7339df10-44ad-419a-9159-977741c917d4","sdu-12a51d09-4995-4b88-9509-f8df2b160d61"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Diagnostic test accuracy study of a commercially available deep learning algorithm for ischemic lesion detection on brain MRIs in suspected stroke patients from a non-comprehensive stroke center","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-704573","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The first patient was misclassified in the diagnostic conclusion according to a local clinical expert opinion in a new clinical implementation of a knee osteoarthritis artificial intelligence (AI) algorithm at Bispebjerg-Frederiksberg University Hospital, Copenhagen, Denmark. In preparation for the evaluation of the AI algorithm, the implementation team collaborated with internal and external partners to plan workflows, and the algorithm was externally validated. After the misclassification, the team was left wondering: what is an acceptable error rate for a low-risk AI diagnostic algorithm? A survey among employees at the Department of Radiology showed significantly lower acceptable error rates for AI (6.8 %) than humans (11.3 %). A general mistrust of AI could cause the discrepancy in acceptable errors. AI may have the disadvantage of limited social capital and likeability compared to human co-workers, and therefore, less potential for forgiveness. Future AI development and implementation require further investigation of the fear of AI's unknown errors to enhance the trustworthiness of perceiving AI as a co-worker. Benchmark tools, transparency, and explainability are also needed to evaluate AI algorithms in clinical implementations to ensure acceptable performance.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lenskjold, Anders","Nybing, Janus Uhd","Trampedach, Charlotte","Galsgaard, Astrid Krabbe-Juelsbo","Brejnebøl, Mathias Willadsen","Raaschou, Henriette","Rose, Martin Høyer","Boesen, Mikael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749245"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Charlie Tango"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"should artificial intelligence have lower acceptable error rates than humans","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1259/bjro.20220053","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749245","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10301708","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37389001","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105000187142","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d72acbb9-aadf-417c-9fdb-fbcd69ea6680"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BB6B4E244789379659B5ABF2E6986D94"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/419114865/bjro.20220053.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1259/bjro.20220053","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Psychology, Department of Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Charlie Tango"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"lenskjoldpau","last":"Lenskjold","name":"Lenskjold, Anders","ra